                "ca94bb5d2f0a0e36d8b895e1d9cd3eb1e1b74c34"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/74/88974/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                "username": "geissonator"
            },
            "createdOn": 1777395156,
            "author": {
                "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                "username": "geissonator"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "FYI it is possible this call could fail at this point in time.\n\nThe power control application may not yet have been able to determine the initial power state of a chassis. In that situation, it will not publish anything on D-Bus for that chassis, rather than just guessing.\n\nThis could happen in situations like the following:\n- The Present property is not (yet?) on D-Bus for that chassis. This property is required for the power control application to know whether it can communicate with the chassis. If the power good signal is obtained from a GPIO, and the chassis is missing, it is hardware implementation-dependent whether attempting to read from the GPIO would fail, produce an invalid value, etc.\n- Communication is not possible to the chassis due to a hardware issue. If the Available property is being used to indicate whether communication is possible, this property could be false or not published on D-Bus (yet?).\n\nThe power control application may publish the pgood property later, such as if the Present or Available property becomes available later. So you could add a listener.\n\nYou can also obviously just assume a pgood value if this call fails, but it will be a random guess."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, we had a similar issue with the skeleton implementation. There's a catch on an error here down below and a fail path where we just assume Off. We'll be listening for it to show up. The look at the Present property (and eventual use of Available) will keep us from doing anything with the chassis."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 101,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: there is an overload that accepts `object_path` directly\n```suggestion\n        \"org.openbmc.control.Power\", powerControlPath, PROPERTY_INTERFACE,\n```\n\nsorry, i should have probably commented this on my first review"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 101,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/xyz.openbmc_project.State.Chassis@.service",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Why did this change? I don't have a problem with it I'm just curious. I believe this service file invokes skeleton code? Not sure on the repercussions of changing it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/xyz.openbmc_project.State.Chassis@.service",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point, the pgood gpio can be hosted in 2 different services. This one and phosphor-power-control.service. Let me change this back and add the power service so whichever one is installed, we'll wait for."
                }
            ],
